[],"nat":{"low":"64","high":"64"},"solution":"<p>64 (63 - 65)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/abe8a5af1baea4d5c9a0dcab85e9e64f3cc852c3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A transmission line has parameters, <img src=\"/media/12d19009c2660d98ac943c6247278e971c4562ec.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /><br />\nThen the characteristic impedance of dc transmission line is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4.47 Ω</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 521.62 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 289.5 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 377 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/19b15e03b5019ff7a8eb8057784b0d144d5dc513.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A civilian radar has a maximum range of 30 kms. The maximum range if the equivalent echoing area becomes 50 times is _________ km.</p>\n<p>(upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"79.77","high":"79.77"},"solution":"<p>79.77 (79.00 - 81.00)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/6a9534b331aa8de86b1ca7e779a38f270e32a548.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For a certain transmission line, the return loss is 13 dB. Then the VSWR on the line is _________.<br />\n(upto three decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.574","high":"1.574"},"solution":"<p>1.574 (0.900 - 2.000)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c2a0fa5a9f0dd85d5bcdc10fe229bd27429ca1db.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the transmission line with characteristic impedance of 50 Ω terminated by a load of <em>j</em> 50 Ω as shown below. The line is exicited by a 30 MHz source.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/06c89e87769596e8de3adb5e1963f976c1248a71.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The distance of the first voltage maxima from the load towards source is __________.</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 75 cm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 100 cm</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 125 cm</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 150 cm</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a6c9c50e4d5a18e6187021dd25ba136c6c34ed81.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>For a certain transmission line, <em>R</em> = 1.5 Ω/m, <em>G</em> = 0.2 mS/m, <em>L</em> = 2.5 nH/m, <em>C</em> = 0.1 pF/m.<br />\nAssume low loss transmission line, then the value of attenuation constant is equal to ________ Np/m.<br />\n(upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.02","high":"0.02"},"solution":"<p>0.02 (0.01 - 0.03)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a68b448ce5dbcc3cf92117e7cee98fe49ae978ef.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider an air-filled rectangular waveguide with <em>a</em> = 6 cm and <em>b</em> = 9 cm. The y component of the<br />\nTEmn mmode is <img src=\"/media/897747b50a08597c06ed15b94bd250b6bc62fa49.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The intrinsic impedance is _________ Ω.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"380.82","high":"380.82"},"solution":"<p>380.82 (379 - 382)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a8f9bb2fccfa7c8141ec04098d3b9d2aa5b92b5d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8340808aaad55ff396c279a52fe6f0e4fab3a033.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>An air filled rectangular waveguide having TE<sub>10</sub> mode as dominant mode is having a cutoff frequency of 18 GHz for TE<sub>30</sub> mode. The inner broad wall dimension of the waveguide is ________ cm. (upto 1 decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.5","high":"2.5"},"solution":"<p>2.5 (1.5 - 3.0)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3a7afcee31a7eb946f72698b876bb8614a86439c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/72baecae509be2ccb096b013f62001f657611b36.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Two identical antennas, each of input impedance 100 Ω are fed with 3 identical quarter wave lines as shown. The input impedance at the source end is ______ Ω. (Assume Z<sub>0</sub> = 50 Ω for all lines)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"200","high":"200"},"solution":"<p>200 (199 - 201)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/288c87c8f85e203267e107d5034c73b2ad8e0c2a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The magnetic field component of a time harmonic plane EM wave travelling in a lossless medium (∈<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 4, μ<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 1) has an amplitude of 1 A/m. The time average power density is equal to _________<br />\nW/m<sup>2</sup>. (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"94.25","high":"94.25"},"solution":"<p>94.25 (93.00 - 95.50)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/df3437d82f4633b5b981c77cd0ffe3ce847e471a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":22,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/23c3e6de92813dbcb40af1d52c6d57d7001dac92.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Consider the rectangular waveguide shown in the above figure. If <em>b</em> > <em>a</em>, the dominant mode of the waveguide is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> TE<sub>10</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> TE<sub>01</sub></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> TM<sub>01</sub></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Both (b) and (c)</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b369607d7886a5e997bddb4c73fcb8e9004aae95.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":23,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The radius of a circular loop Antenna is 0.02λ. The number of turns of Antenna required to give a radiation resistance of 35 Ω is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 13</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 21</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 27</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 35</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ebed9c05143ae609b0155b4a9e96e53d9a43da0e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d07fea128ba20ffb79ffdab163b19203e7fd09b7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>An end-fire array consisting of several half wavelength long isotropic radiators is to have a directive gain of 30. Beam width between first nulls (BWFN) is given by _________ degrees (upto one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"59.8","high":"59.8"},"solution":"<p>59.8 (58.0 - 61.0)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e8fd7c647d4b9a6ed51210f2dac4b95195797464.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"NAT","correc